>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `FAST_TAC`

``` hol4
classicalLib.FAST_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Solves a goal by depth-first classical search.

`FAST_TAC thms` repeatedly saturates the state with safe reasoning, then
searches the first open goal. It tries instantiating rules before unsafe
rules and commits to the instantiating family whenever that family has a
candidate. Search uses dynamic pruning when choices made while solving one
goal cannot affect the remaining goals. It has no numeric depth or node
bound and can therefore diverge.

The theorem list modifies the current classical rule set for this call.
The markers `SIntro`, `Intro`, `SElim`, `Elim`, `SDest`, `Dest` and `Del`
add or remove rules. Every unmarked theorem is inserted as an assumption
before search starts. Content-bearing generic simplifier wrappers such as
`Once th` are unwrapped and inserted; inert controls such as `Cong`, `Excl`
and `SF` are ignored. No change survives the call.

Unlike `SAFE_TAC`, this is a solve-completely tactic: a successful result
has no residual goals.

### Failure

Fails if depth-first search does not find and replay a complete proof.
Search may diverge instead of failing. Malformed extra rules can also fail
while the theorem list is processed.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem fast_tac_example:
  (?x. x = a) /\ (p \/ ~p)
Proof
  classicalLib.FAST_TAC []
QED
```

